 "styleRules": [
  "True-scale realistic silhouettes (1 stud = 0.28 m) built from a few chunky volumes; never alpha cards, photo textures or texture noise.",
  "Flat-shaded facets sized to the object: 1-2.5 studs on trees and buildings, 0.5-1.5 on rocks and props, nothing under ~0.1 stud except trim.",
  "Foliage is closed faceted volumes: conifers as drooping star-lobed tiers, broadleaf as flat-bottomed convex-hull clumps on visible branches; trunks are tapered 7-9-sided prisms with root flare.",
  "Colour is painted, not detailed: dark inside/underneath to light tips/tops, +-6% per volume and +-3% per facet, slight warm/cool hue drift.",
  "One baked set per asset (Color/Normal/Roughness, 512-1024 px, ~10-25 px/stud): two-radius AO multiplied into Color at 60-78%; the normal map only rounds edges (bevel 0.03-0.12) plus broad bark plates or adze dimples.",
  "Built things are assembled from real members: octagonal hewn logs with chamfers, proud corner ends and recessed chinking; plank-by-plank decks; single fieldstones with mortar gaps; shingles as staggered tilted strips.",
  "Muted mid-value palette: needles 26-98 green, leaves 30-108, bark 66-114, weathered wood 96-132, stone 93-146, chinking ~165; no pure black/white, no saturated accents on world assets.",
  "Matte surfaces (roughness 0.8-0.95, metal 0) so Roblox Realistic lighting and cast shadows do the shading; glass is the only glossy surface.",
  "Terrain tiles are modelled at true scale from discrete shapes (rounded pebbles, folded leaves, duff flakes, twigs, moss) with soft contact AO and low value contrast, so they stay calm at distance; seamless, 8-10 StudsPerTile.",
  "Budgets: trees 3.5-5k tris, cabin ~16k split by collision part (each <5k), boulders <300; pipeline collision rules (Hull trunks/roofs/rocks, PreciseConvexDecomposition walls and climbable limbs, canopies non-colliding)."
 ],
